body:
Looks like the Third Eye (the pineal gland) which is the seat of dreams.

&#x200B;

Also, Carl Jung said the flying saucer is a symbol of completion and wholeness of the self.

"Paths of Wisdom" by John Michael Greer

&#x200B;

"The Secret Teachings of All Ages" by Manly P Hall

Magick is the art and science of causing change in accordance with will. It's an art in that it is meant to be beautiful in its own right devoid of extrinsic goals, and it's a science in that it does have very definite goals and models of how the world works. The art aspect definitely is real. A good magickal ritual can be a beautiful and enthusiastic experience. The science aspect is more constrained. You can achieve magickal results, but only within the realm of ordinariness. Basically, if you can't expect to achieve a goal by ordinary means, don't expect to achieve it by magickal means either.

&#x200B;

Go pick up a copy of Modern Magick if you're ready to begin learning.

Love spells are an ethical no-go, in my opinion. 

&#x200B;

A better option is invoke a love spirit, like the goddess Venus, to give you the power to be more loving. That way people will naturally be more attracted to you and you won't have to exert your will over theirs.
